    "type": "question",
    "label": "34",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$\\frac{x}{x+1}+\\frac2{x-2}=1.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-4$.",
      "worked": "$x\\ne-1,2$. Multiply by $(x+1)(x-2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x-2)+2(x+1)&=(x+1)(x-2)\\\\x^2+2&=x^2-x-2\\\\x+4&=0\\\\x&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nThis value is admissible.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
